cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the datasets, Python scripts, modelling outputs,
  or methodological framework from this repository,
  please cite this repository and the associated research
  publication when available.

type: software

title: >-
  Qatar Water Distribution Vulnerability
  Framework (WDVF)

authors:
  - family-names: More
    given-names: Kagiso S.

abstract: >-
  This repository provides research datasets, Python scripts,
  climate projections, modelling outputs, and supporting
  documentation for an integrated GIS-AI assessment of
  municipal water distribution vulnerability in Qatar.
  The framework combines groundwater hydrochemistry,
  historical and projected hydroclimatic stress,
  hydraulic susceptibility, GIS-based spatial analysis,
  and machine-learning classification. Climate projections
  incorporate ACCESS-CM2 simulations under SSP2-4.5 and
  SSP5-8.5. The computational workflow uses Python 3.13.9
  and includes Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, and XGBoost.

keywords:
  - Municipal water distribution
  - Vulnerability assessment
  - Hydrogeochemistry
  - Hydroclimatic stress
  - Hydraulic modelling
  - Geographic information systems
  - Machine learning
  - Climate change
  - CMIP6
  - Qatar

repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Kagiso-S-More/Qatar_MWDVF

url: >-
